### 12.2 Potential for knowledge and learning

The project involves capacity-building, technical training and enhancement for inter-agency collaboration among all components.

Component I is focused on improving the capacity for generating, communicating and using climate and hydrological information. These goals would be achieved through several actions:

- The provision of hardware and software for enhanced generation of climate and environmental data;
- Technical training to 30 staff from the Thai Meteorological Department (TMD), Royal Irrigation Department (RID) and relevant agencies on integration of climate change into water resources management;
- Development of tailored climate information products and climate forecast models;
- Development of SDPs for sharing of climate information across relevant departments;
- Workshops and meetings for sensitization and collaboration in sharing information and supporting decision-making;

